  "equipment_type": "Air compressor controller",
  "applies_to": "Ingersoll Rand rotary screw air compressors with the Xe-90M or Xe-145M controller on Modbus, read by a BASgatewayLX.",
  "summary": "Gateway profile for the Ingersoll Rand Xe-90M/Xe-145M: 66 objects (44 AI, 10 AO, 9 BI, 3 BO), 58 polled by default. Coils switch host/local, run/stop and load/unload; outputs set online/offline pressures, mode, lead/lag and timers; inputs give modulation, alarm and warning flags, discharge, sump, interstage and remote pressures, temperatures, filter drops, hours and option settings.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "Built from Contemporary Controls' BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile Ingersoll_Rand_XE_90M_XE_145M_a_LX.csv; the profile maps the registers in the Xe-90M / Xe-145M Modbus register list (https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/XeMModbusRegisters.pdf).",
    "Object instances are the ones this profile assigns when it is loaded into the gateway. A site that edited or rebuilt the profile may use different instances.",
    "Only 58 of the 66 rows are flagged for polling in the profile; the rest are served only after you tick them in the gateway. Their descriptions say \"not polled by default\".",
    "The CSV has no read/write column: Analog/Binary Inputs are read-only and Analog/Binary Outputs are commandable (priority array), which is how the gateway maps them (access inferred). Descriptions give the Modbus register each object reads."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile Ingersoll_Rand_XE_90M_XE_145M_a",
    "doc_number": "Ingersoll_Rand_XE_90M_XE_145M_a_LX.csv",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/Ingersoll_Rand_XE_90M_XE_145M_a_LX.zip"
  },
